---
import CoverageGrid from "../CoverageGrid.astro";
import { unseen } from "../../lib/coverage";
import PartHead from "./PartHead.astro";
import NextPart from "./NextPart.astro";
import AiStudy from "./AiStudy.astro";
import { claimsPrompt } from "../../lib/primer";

const report = [
  { key: "rosters", text: "Rosters were collected for all seven schools.", answer: "strike", why: `Strike. Dunmore's roster cell is No collector. Rosters are held for ${unseen.rosters} of 7.` },
  { key: "boxes", text: `Box scores are held for ${unseen.withBox} of ${unseen.held} conference matches, so the 2025 season is missing ${unseen.held - unseen.withBox} box scores.`, answer: "strike", why: `Strike. The first half is true of the file. The second half is a claim about the season, which scheduled ${unseen.expected} matches, so ${unseen.expected - unseen.withBox} of the ${unseen.expected} have no box score in the file. A denominator taken from the run cannot show what the run missed.` },
  { key: "held", text: `No Dunmore page was read for 2025, and the season file still holds ${unseen.dunmoreHeld} Dunmore conference matches.`, answer: "keep", why: `Keep. All ${unseen.dunmoreHeld} came from opponents' pages, and the sentence says how many are held without claiming that is all of them.` },
  { key: "zero", text: "Dunmore's site had no conference matches for 2025.", answer: "strike", why: `Strike. Dunmore's schedule cell is No collector: nothing on its site could be read, so the record can't say what the site holds. The file already holds ${unseen.dunmoreHeld} Dunmore conference matches from opponents' pages.` },
  { key: "why", text: "Eastbrook State's own box-score pages could not be listed, because its schedule could not be verified.", answer: "keep", why: "Keep. The record gives exactly that reason, and the sentence claims nothing about the matches themselves." },
];
---

<section id="prove-it">
  <PartHead id="prove-it">Prove it: the season nobody called about</PartHead>
  <p>Here is Touchline's coverage record for the previous season: Prairie Lakes men, 2025. Hartwell Tech hadn't joined yet, and the conference used the same format. Conference matches are missing from this season too, and no coach called about them.</p>
  <p>In the original Friday run, Riley's readers found the gaps. Riley can check the coverage record for those gaps <em>before</em> publishing. Tap the incomplete squares below to read what happened.</p>
  <CoverageGrid rows={unseen.grid} caption="Coverage record, Prairie Lakes men, 2025" id="past" />

  <h4 class="cv-try">Red-pen the report</h4>
  <p>The 2025 season file contains {unseen.held} conference matches, with box scores for {unseen.withBox} of them. Of the {unseen.held}, {unseen.dunmoreHeld} involve Dunmore, all read from opponents' schedule pages. Kick drafted five statements about the season. Answer the first question, then mark each statement <strong>Keep</strong> if the record supports it, or <strong>Strike</strong> if it doesn't.</p>
  <div class="cv-check" data-once="report">
    <p class="cv-kind">Assessment</p>
    <div data-q data-type="number" data-answer={unseen.expected} data-why={`${unseen.expected}. Seven schools each host the other six: 7 × 6, from the membership list and competition format.`}>
      <label for="cv-expected">How many conference matches did the 2025 format schedule?</label>
      <input id="cv-expected" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" data-save="q-expected" />
      <p class="cv-fb" role="status"></p>
    </div>
    <div class="cv-draft">
      <div class="cv-chat-bar">
        <span class="cv-agent-badge">Kick · Drafted report</span>
        <span class="cv-chat-meta">5 claims to check</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cv-draft-body">
        {report.map((r) => (
          <fieldset class="cv-line" data-q data-type="radio" data-answer={r.answer} data-why={r.why}>
            <legend>“{r.text}”</legend>
            <label><input type="radio" name={`rep-${r.key}`} value="keep" data-save={`rep-${r.key}`} /><span>Keep</span></label>
            <label><input type="radio" name={`rep-${r.key}`} value="strike" data-save={`rep-${r.key}`} /><span>Strike</span></label>
            <p class="cv-fb" role="status"></p>
          </fieldset>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="cv-once">Answer all six, then check.</p>
    <button type="button" data-submit>Check answers</button>
    <p class="cv-fb" role="status" data-need></p>
    <div class="cv-reveal">
      <ol class="cv-reach is-plain" aria-label="Three counts for the 2025 season">
        <li><b>{unseen.schedules} of 7</b><span>verified schedule pages</span></li>
        <li><b>{unseen.held} of {unseen.expected}</b><span>matches in the file; both Dunmore–Eastbrook State matches missing</span></li>
        <li><b>{unseen.withBox} of {unseen.expected}</b><span>expected matches with a box score in the file</span></li>
      </ol>
      <p>All three counts are true, and each measures something different. “{unseen.withBox} of {unseen.held}” is true of the file, yet misleading if read as the whole season. A count taken from collected data belongs next to the count against the expected set, with the gaps named.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cv-commit" id="prove-caption" data-commit>
    <p class="cv-kind">Write it <span>you check your own</span></p>
    <label class="cv-write" for="cv-caption">Now write the caption that should go under the published 2025 standings table.</label>
    <textarea id="cv-caption" rows="3" placeholder="State the count, the denominator, and the missing matches..." data-save="caption"></textarea>
    <div class="cv-actions">
      <button type="button" data-commit-btn disabled>Compare with example</button>
      <button type="button" class="cv-link-btn" data-commit-skip>Skip and show example</button>
    </div>
    <p class="cv-once" data-needs-note>Write a short sentence to compare, or skip ahead.</p>
    <div class="cv-reveal">
      <p class="cv-model">Counts {unseen.held} of {unseen.expected} conference matches. Not collected: both Dunmore–Eastbrook State matches. Each of those two schools has two more scheduled matches than this table shows.</p>
      <fieldset class="cv-ticks">
        <legend>Review your caption against these three criteria:</legend>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="cap-count" /><span>Gives both the count and the expected total</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="cap-gap" /><span>Names the gap so readers know which rows are incomplete</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="cap-true" /><span>Makes no claims about the two unseen results</span></label>
      </fieldset>
      <AiStudy
        id="prove-ai-study"
        title="Does the record support the sentence?"
        note="Send this prompt to read the reply an AI assistant gave, or copy it into your own. Then come back and compare its better caption with yours."
        prompt={claimsPrompt}
        href="../01-collection-ai-claims/"
      />
    </div>
  </div>
  <NextPart from="prove-it">When would a blank report justify counting zero?</NextPart>
</section>
